From: BigCherry <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] engine: drain each rank's mover queue before its arena is freed at shutdown

Ctx::shutdown() synchronises the compute stream and lane 1, then releases the activation arena.
The mover's transfer queue is drained only later, in Mover::~Mover. A promotion into an
arena-lent slab slot, or a prefill-stager copy into the arena top, still queued at shutdown then
writes freed memory: sq_intr MEMVIOL on gfx1100 and a wedged queue on rank 0 (the first to shut
down). Seen as aql_copy_link hangs after the last request in Flash-Next two-XTX runs.

diff --git a/core/engine.cpp b/core/engine.cpp
index 3ba2831..20767f7 100644
--- a/core/engine.cpp
+++ b/core/engine.cpp
@@ -79,7 +79,13 @@ Engine::~Engine() {
                  (unsigned long long)r->ctx.route_dropped());
         RAD_INFO("%s", r->mover.report().c_str());
     }
-    for (auto& r : ranks_) r->ctx.shutdown();
+    for (auto& r : ranks_) {
+        /* The mover copies into arena-lent slab slots and the prefill stager's buffers at the
+         * arena top: drain it before the arena below is freed. */
+        if (rad_dev_set(r->device) >= 0)
+            if (RadStream s = r->mover.transfer_stream()) rad_stream_sync(s);
+        r->ctx.shutdown();
+    }
     step_state_fini();
     ranks_.clear();
     for (TableCopy& c : table_copies_) table_copy_free(&c);
